# Release secrets (maintainer only)

Copy to `docs/RELEASE.local.md` (gitignored) and configure these GitHub repository secrets before running the Release workflow.

## Required for signed releases

| Secret | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `APPLE_CERTIFICATE_BASE64` | Base64-encoded `.p12` export of your **Developer ID Application** certificate (include private key) |
| `APPLE_CERTIFICATE_PASSWORD` | Password used when exporting the `.p12` |
| `APPLE_TEAM_ID` | Apple Developer team ID (e.g. `8B8983VEMG`) |
| `APPLE_ID` | Apple ID email used for notarization |
| `APPLE_NOTARIZATION_PASSWORD` | App-specific password for notarization ([appleid.apple.com](https://appleid.apple.com)) |

## Optional

| Secret | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `RELEASE_NOTES_API_KEY` | OpenAI API key for AI-generated release notes |

## Export certificate as base64

```bash
base64 -i ~/Downloads/Certificates.p12 | pbcopy
# Paste into GitHub → Settings → Secrets → APPLE_CERTIFICATE_BASE64
```

## Why signing is required

Unsigned macOS apps **cannot receive Screen Recording** on macOS 15+. System Settings may show Cue as enabled, but the app will never get permission. Release DMGs must be Developer ID signed (and notarized for smooth install).

## Local signed release test

```bash
export RELEASE_SIGN=1
export DEVELOPMENT_TEAM=YOUR_TEAM_ID
./scripts/build-release.sh
```

With notarization:

```bash
export RELEASE_SIGN=1
export NOTARIZE_RELEASE=1
export DEVELOPMENT_TEAM=YOUR_TEAM_ID
export APPLE_ID=you@example.com
export APPLE_NOTARIZATION_PASSWORD=xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx
./scripts/build-release.sh
```
